0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(1. Why does TCP use a three-way handshake?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - It establishes synchronized sequence numbers and confirms both sides are) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     ready to communicate reliably.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Which mode had lower response time?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Persistent mode showed lower average response time.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. Why does new-connection mode have more overhead?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Every message requires handshake and teardown packets, adding delay and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     control traffic.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. Which mode is better for CampusChat and why?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Persistent mode, because chat is interactive and benefits from avoiding) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     repeated connect overhead.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(5. Which mode is suitable for NetAttend and why?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - New-connection mode can be suitable for short periodic updates where each) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     request is independent and server state can stay simple.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(6. How does message size affect throughput?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Throughput increases with message size because protocol overhead is) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     amortized over larger payloads.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
